The Nautilus DevOps team is delving into Kubernetes for app management. 
One team member needs to create a deployment following these details:

Create a deployment named nginx to deploy the application nginx using the image nginx:latest (ensure to specify the tag)

Note: The kubectl utility on the jump-host has been configured to work with the Kubernetes cluster.

SOLUTION
Create the nginx Deployment
Here's the YAML manifest and the steps to create the deployment as specified.

Deployment YAML Manifest
yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:latest
Steps to Create the Deployment
Option 1: Apply using a YAML file (recommended)
Create the manifest file:

bash
cat <<EOF > nginx-deployment.yaml
apiVersion: apps/v1
kind: Deployment
metadata:
  name: nginx
  labels:
    app: nginx
spec:
  replicas: 1
  selector:
    matchLabels:
      app: nginx
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        app: nginx
    spec:
      containers:
      - name: nginx
        image: nginx:latest
EOF
Apply it:

bash
kubectl apply -f nginx-deployment.yaml
Option 2: Imperative command
bash
kubectl create deployment nginx --image=nginx:latest
Note: The imperative command works fine and defaults to 1 replica. Just make sure the image tag is explicitly nginx:latest (don't omit the tag), since omitting it would default to latest implicitly — but the task requires it to be explicitly specified.

Verification
Confirm the deployment was created correctly:

bash
# Check deployment status
kubectl get deployment nginx

# Check the rollout status
kubectl rollout status deployment/nginx

# Verify image tag
kubectl get deployment nginx -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[*].image}{"\n"}'

# Check that pods are running (managed by the deployment)
kubectl get pods -l app=nginx

# Get detailed info
kubectl describe deployment nginx
Expected output for the image check:

text
nginx:latest
Expected deployment status:

text
NAME    READY   UP-TO-DATE   AVAILABLE   AGE
nginx   1/1     1            1           XXs
Summary of Requirements Met
Requirement	Value
Deployment name	nginx
Application	nginx
Image	nginx:latest (tag explicitly specified)
The deployment is now created and manages a pod running nginx:latest. You can scale it later with kubectl scale deployment nginx --replicas=<n> if needed.
